---
export const prerender = false;

/**
 * GONE, AND STILL ANSWERING.
 *
 * This listed every warning a program had collected, in one raw list. Two
 * things were wrong with it. Nobody reads a page of advice before they need
 * any of it, and once they do need it they are looking for one line about
 * one step, which a list ordered by program and date is the wrong shape for
 * finding.
 *
 * The warnings themselves were never the problem and are not gone. They are
 * written on a step and shown on that step, beside the work they are warning
 * about, which is the only moment they are worth reading. Confirming one for
 * the season and retiring one that has stopped being true moved there too,
 * because a judgment about whether advice still holds is made looking at the
 * advice.
 *
 * The route survives as a redirect rather than as a 404, for the reason
 * `/app/fairs/` does: a dead link is a worse answer than a moved one.
 */
return Astro.redirect('/app/', 301);
---
